# The stem's files this node carries MODIFIED, each with the reason it differs.
#
# WHAT THIS IS FOR. `.offshoot-omissions` lists what this repo does not carry
# from its stem (jolly-roger `main`); this lists what it carries and changes.
# Everything else is the stem's byte for byte or this repo's own, so a diff
# against the stem reads as: the additions, the omissions (listed there) and
# these. A modified file is a conflict on every cascade that touches it, so
# each one here is a cost paid on purpose, and the reason says what it buys. A
# cascade reviewer meeting one of these files knows the node's side is a
# decision; meeting any other modified file, it is drift.
#
# AND IT IS CHECKED, by `scripts/check-divergences.mjs` (the tree's one copy,
# from template-svelte), run by `web/test/offshoot-divergences.test.ts` and by
# `scripts/apply-omissions.sh` during a merge: it fails on a modified file with
# no entry, on an entry whose file no longer differs, and on an entry with no
# reason. A file at the stem's OLD version is drift, not a divergence:
# `scripts/check-stem-drift.mjs` catches that.
#
# FORMAT. One file per line: its path, then its reason. `#` starts a comment.
# A line `[<branch>]` starts a section.
#
# SECTIONS, AND HOW THIS FILE CASCADES. This section, with no marker, is
# `main`'s: what jolly-roger `main` modifies from template-svelte-shadcn
# `main`. Each other branch of this repo inherits it by merge, as it inherits
# `.offshoot-omissions`, and adds its own entries below a `[<its branch>]`
# marker: what IT modifies from its own stem branch. Only the last section is
# checked at a node; the sections above are its stems', checked there. A child
# REPO (template-commit-reveal, bleeps, mandalas, template-zk-game) never keeps
# these entries: its list is its own, written against this repo, and until it
# writes one it carries this file unchanged and the check says it has none.

